  planner_response {
    response: "The preview matches the code logic in **`src/App.tsx`**, which uses an **authentication gate**:\n\n### 1. Why you see the Login screen first\nIn `src/App.tsx` (lines 30\342\200\22340 & 216\342\200\223218):\n```tsx\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<AuthUser | null>(() => {\n  const saved = localStorage.getItem(LOCAL_STORAGE_USER_KEY);\n  return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : null;\n});\n\nif (!user) {\n  return <LoginPanel onLogin={(userObj) => setUser(userObj)} />;\n}\n```\nWhen first loading the app, no user session exists in `localStorage`, so the app displays the **`LoginPanel`** component by default.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to view the Main Trading Dashboard & Charts\nYou can enter the journal in two ways:\n1. **Instant Access (Demo Trader)**: Click **\"Try Demo Trader (Instant Access)\"** on the login screen.\n2. **Sign In**: Enter any email/password to create an isolated trader profile (or connect your Supabase database via the settings cog).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Loading Sample Trades & Analytics\nOnce logged in:\n- If your account is new, click **\"Reset / Sample Data\"** in the top navigation bar to populate the dashboard with sample trades, win/loss distributions, and P&L charts.\n- You can switch between the **Trade Log** table and **Analytics & Charts** view using the top navigation tabs.\n\n---\n\n*If you would like the application to automatically bypass the login screen and boot directly into the active trading dashboard by default, please let me know and I can configure that for you!*"
    thinking: "**Clarifying Application Startup**\n\nI\'m currently investigating the application\'s startup behavior. Specifically, I\'m trying to determine the user\'s expectations. Are they looking for immediate access to the main dashboard, bypassing a login screen, or are they wondering why the login screen appears at all. I\'ll need to clearly explain the code\'s current functionality related to this startup process.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The preview matches the code logic in **`src/App.tsx`**, which uses an **authentication gate**:\n\n### 1. Why you see the Login screen first\nIn `src/App.tsx` (lines 30\342\200\22340 & 216\342\200\223218):\n```tsx\nconst [user, setUser] = useState<AuthUser | null>(() => {\n  const saved = localStorage.getItem(LOCAL_STORAGE_USER_KEY);\n  return saved ? JSON.parse(saved) : null;\n});\n\nif (!user) {\n  return <LoginPanel onLogin={(userObj) => setUser(userObj)} />;\n}\n```\nWhen first loading the app, no user session exists in `localStorage`, so the app displays the **`LoginPanel`** component by default.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to view the Main Trading Dashboard & Charts\nYou can enter the journal in two ways:\n1. **Instant Access (Demo Trader)**: Click **\"Try Demo Trader (Instant Access)\"** on the login screen.\n2. **Sign In**: Enter any email/password to create an isolated trader profile (or connect your Supabase database via the settings cog).\n\n---\n\n### 3. Loading Sample Trades & Analytics\nOnce logged in:\n- If your account is new, click **\"Reset / Sample Data\"** in the top navigation bar to populate the dashboard with sample trades, win/loss distributions, and P&L charts.\n- You can switch between the **Trade Log** table and **Analytics & Charts** view using the top navigation tabs.\n\n---\n\n*If you would like the application to automatically bypass the login screen and boot directly into the active trading dashboard by default, please let me know and I can configure that for you!*"
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 607732185
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
