  planner_response {
    response: "Here is how **Google Auth + Notion Database** works together seamlessly:\n\n---\n\n### How Google Authentication works with Notion\n\nBecause **Notion itself is a database** (and does not manage your user passwords or logins directly), you have two clean, modern options:\n\n#### **Option A: Direct Google One-Tap / OAuth Sign-In (Recommended)**\n- Users click **\"Sign in with Google\"** via official Google Identity Services (GSI).\n- Once signed in with Google, your trading journal loads your private Notion Database.\n- You get instant, password-free login with your Google account while all your trade data lives inside Notion.\n\n#### **Option B: Notion OAuth Login (Log in with Notion)**\n- Users click **\"Connect with Notion\"**.\n- Notion prompts you to log in (which supports **\"Continue with Google\"** directly inside Notion\'s prompt).\n- This grants the app instant permission to read & write to your Notion trading journal database.\n\n#### **Option C: Personal Private Mode (Single-User Journal)**\n- If this is your personal journal, you configure your Notion integration token, and you can protect access with **Google Sign-In** so only your Google email (`bhainirdesh92@gmail.com`) can access and modify your Notion database.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n- You **do NOT need Supabase** for Google Auth.\n- You can have **Google Sign-In + Notion Database** working together.\n- All your trade entries, chart screenshots, setups (`DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, `T.C. QML A+`, `DB`, `DT`), and notes will sync to your Notion table.\n\nWould you like me to implement **Google Sign-In + Notion Database** for the app?"
    modified_response: "Here is how **Google Auth + Notion Database** works together seamlessly:\n\n---\n\n### How Google Authentication works with Notion\n\nBecause **Notion itself is a database** (and does not manage your user passwords or logins directly), you have two clean, modern options:\n\n#### **Option A: Direct Google One-Tap / OAuth Sign-In (Recommended)**\n- Users click **\"Sign in with Google\"** via official Google Identity Services (GSI).\n- Once signed in with Google, your trading journal loads your private Notion Database.\n- You get instant, password-free login with your Google account while all your trade data lives inside Notion.\n\n#### **Option B: Notion OAuth Login (Log in with Notion)**\n- Users click **\"Connect with Notion\"**.\n- Notion prompts you to log in (which supports **\"Continue with Google\"** directly inside Notion\'s prompt).\n- This grants the app instant permission to read & write to your Notion trading journal database.\n\n#### **Option C: Personal Private Mode (Single-User Journal)**\n- If this is your personal journal, you configure your Notion integration token, and you can protect access with **Google Sign-In** so only your Google email (`bhainirdesh92@gmail.com`) can access and modify your Notion database.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n- You **do NOT need Supabase** for Google Auth.\n- You can have **Google Sign-In + Notion Database** working together.\n- All your trade entries, chart screenshots, setups (`DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, `T.C. QML A+`, `DB`, `DT`), and notes will sync to your Notion table.\n\nWould you like me to implement **Google Sign-In + Notion Database** for the app?"
