  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Notion Endpoints**\n\nOkay, here\'s the deal: I\'m currently focused on fleshing out the Notion endpoints within `server.ts` using the `@notionhq/client` library. Right now, I\'m building out a `GET /api/notion/status` endpoint. It\'ll return a JSON payload with the configuration status, a database ID, any errors, and the database title. Also, working on a `POST /api/notion/test-connection` endpoint to test connectivity.\n\n\n**Expanding Notion Integration**\n\nI\'ve made good progress expanding the Notion integration. I\'ve designed several endpoints: `GET /api/notion/trades` to read trade data, `POST /api/notion/trades` for inserting new trades, `PATCH /api/notion/trades/:id` for updating existing trades, and `DELETE /api/notion/trades/:id` to archive trades, which will be the update. The focus is now on flexibly handling various property names and types users might employ in their Notion databases to ensure seamless functionality, no matter the specific schema.\n\n\n"
