  planner_response {
    response: "**You can do both! They are synced together in real time.**\n\nBecause we built a **two-way integration**, you can choose whichever workflow is most convenient for you at any given moment:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: Log directly inside Notion\n* If you are on your phone or working directly inside your Notion workspace, you can create new rows in your Notion Trading Journal database table.\n* **What happens**: Whenever you open this web app, it reads and queries your Notion database, pulling in your new trades, calculating your risk-reward ratios, and updating your win rate charts.\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Log inside this Web App\n* You can click **\"+ New Trade\"** in this app to take advantage of:\n  * **Automated Calculations**: Pip risk, position sizing, planned vs. actual R:R, and profit/loss calculated for you automatically.\n  * **Strategy Selectors**: Quick single-click selection for **DEMAND**, **SUPPLY**, **T.C QML**, **T.C. QML A+**, **DB**, and **DT**.\n  * **Emotional Tracking**: Psychology and discipline tags.\n  * **Screenshot Uploads**: Attaching TradingView chart images directly.\n* **What happens**: The app writes the trade directly to your Notion database page instantaneously.\n\n---\n\n### Why using both together gives you the best of both worlds:\n1. **Notion gives you**: Permanent cloud storage, mobile app access, rich text notes, and integration with your broader workspace.\n2. **This App gives you**: \n   - **Interactive Visual Charts** (cumulative PnL equity curve, win/loss breakdown, strategy win rate % comparison).\n   - **Risk Analytics** (Sharpe ratio, expectancy, average win vs. loss).\n   - **AI Trading Coach / Auditor** (analyzing your trading discipline and psychological patterns with Gemini)."
