  planner_response {
    response: "**Yes! By using your Notion Database, you effectively have unlimited storage for your trading journal.**\n\nHere is exactly how the storage limits work:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Unlimited Trade Records in Notion\n* **Free & Plus Notion plans** allow **unlimited pages/blocks** in personal workspaces.\n* You can log **thousands of trades** across years of trading (`EUR/USD`, `XAU/USD`, `DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, etc.) without hitting database capacity limits.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chart Screenshots & Image Storage\n* **Notion Database**: Notion natively stores your uploaded chart files, images, and notes.\n* **External Links**: If you paste TradingView chart snapshot URLs (e.g. `tradingview.com/x/...`), they take up virtually zero storage and can be embedded endlessly.\n* **Notion File Uploads**: Free Notion accounts have a 5MB per individual file upload limit, which is more than enough for chart screenshots (TradingView screenshots are typically under 1MB). Plus/Pro Notion accounts have unlimited file sizes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. No Third-Party Database Fees or Quotas\n* Unlike services with strict row limits on free tiers (like Supabase, Firebase free tiers, or Cloud SQL), **Notion is your dedicated cloud host**.\n* You don\'t have to worry about monthly database subscription bills, storage expirations, or quota resets.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nYour trades, setups, calculations, screenshots, and psychological reviews are stored directly in your **Notion workspace**, giving you complete ownership and unlimited journal entries."
    modified_response: "**Yes! By using your Notion Database, you effectively have unlimited storage for your trading journal.**\n\nHere is exactly how the storage limits work:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Unlimited Trade Records in Notion\n* **Free & Plus Notion plans** allow **unlimited pages/blocks** in personal workspaces.\n* You can log **thousands of trades** across years of trading (`EUR/USD`, `XAU/USD`, `DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, etc.) without hitting database capacity limits.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Chart Screenshots & Image Storage\n* **Notion Database**: Notion natively stores your uploaded chart files, images, and notes.\n* **External Links**: If you paste TradingView chart snapshot URLs (e.g. `tradingview.com/x/...`), they take up virtually zero storage and can be embedded endlessly.\n* **Notion File Uploads**: Free Notion accounts have a 5MB per individual file upload limit, which is more than enough for chart screenshots (TradingView screenshots are typically under 1MB). Plus/Pro Notion accounts have unlimited file sizes.\n\n---\n\n### 3. No Third-Party Database Fees or Quotas\n* Unlike services with strict row limits on free tiers (like Supabase, Firebase free tiers, or Cloud SQL), **Notion is your dedicated cloud host**.\n* You don\'t have to worry about monthly database subscription bills, storage expirations, or quota resets.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nYour trades, setups, calculations, screenshots, and psychological reviews are stored directly in your **Notion workspace**, giving you complete ownership and unlimited journal entries."
