  planner_response {
    response: "**Important Note on Hosting this Application:**\n\nBecause this application uses a **secure backend server (`server.ts` with Node.js/Express)** to talk safely to the **Notion API** and **Gemini AI** (protecting your secret `NOTION_API_KEY` and `GEMINI_API_KEY` so they are never exposed to browser visitors):\n\n---\n\n### Can you use GitHub Pages (e.g. `username.github.io`)?\n- **GitHub Pages ONLY hosts static HTML/JS files (frontend-only).** It cannot run a Node.js Express backend.\n- If you deploy purely to GitHub Pages, your backend API endpoints (`/api/notion/*`, `/api/ai-insights`) won\'t run.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Options for Live 24/7 Hosting:\n\n#### **Option 1: Deploy Directly with Google AI Studio / Cloud Run (Easiest & Free)**\n* Click the **Deploy** or **Share** button directly in the AI Studio menu bar.\n* It provisions a live Cloud Run URL (like `https://ais-pre-...run.app` or a custom domain) with full server support automatically.\n\n#### **Option 2: GitHub Repository + Free Full-Stack Hosting Platform**\nPush your code to a GitHub repo, and connect it with 1 click to any of these free Node.js hosting providers:\n1. **Render** ([render.com](https://render.com)) \342\200\223 Free Node.js Web Service (connects directly to your GitHub repository).\n2. **Vercel** ([vercel.com](https://vercel.com)) \342\200\223 Supports serverless API routes.\n3. **Railway** ([railway.app](https://railway.app)) \342\200\223 One-click deploy from GitHub.\n4. **Fly.io** ([fly.io](https://fly.io)) \342\200\223 Free container hosting.\n\n---\n\n### If You Have a Custom Domain (e.g. `yourname.com` or `journal.yourdomain.com`):\n- You can point your custom domain to any of the above platforms (Render, Vercel, Cloud Run) for free with automatic SSL/HTTPS certificates.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Checklist for Live Hosting:\n1. Keep the code in a **GitHub repository** (for version control and easy syncing).\n2. Deploy to a platform that supports Node.js (Cloud Run, Render, Vercel, or Railway).\n3. Add your environment variables (`NOTION_API_KEY`, `NOTION_DATABASE_ID`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) in the hosting dashboard."
    modified_response: "**Important Note on Hosting this Application:**\n\nBecause this application uses a **secure backend server (`server.ts` with Node.js/Express)** to talk safely to the **Notion API** and **Gemini AI** (protecting your secret `NOTION_API_KEY` and `GEMINI_API_KEY` so they are never exposed to browser visitors):\n\n---\n\n### Can you use GitHub Pages (e.g. `username.github.io`)?\n- **GitHub Pages ONLY hosts static HTML/JS files (frontend-only).** It cannot run a Node.js Express backend.\n- If you deploy purely to GitHub Pages, your backend API endpoints (`/api/notion/*`, `/api/ai-insights`) won\'t run.\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Options for Live 24/7 Hosting:\n\n#### **Option 1: Deploy Directly with Google AI Studio / Cloud Run (Easiest & Free)**\n* Click the **Deploy** or **Share** button directly in the AI Studio menu bar.\n* It provisions a live Cloud Run URL (like `https://ais-pre-...run.app` or a custom domain) with full server support automatically.\n\n#### **Option 2: GitHub Repository + Free Full-Stack Hosting Platform**\nPush your code to a GitHub repo, and connect it with 1 click to any of these free Node.js hosting providers:\n1. **Render** ([render.com](https://render.com)) \342\200\223 Free Node.js Web Service (connects directly to your GitHub repository).\n2. **Vercel** ([vercel.com](https://vercel.com)) \342\200\223 Supports serverless API routes.\n3. **Railway** ([railway.app](https://railway.app)) \342\200\223 One-click deploy from GitHub.\n4. **Fly.io** ([fly.io](https://fly.io)) \342\200\223 Free container hosting.\n\n---\n\n### If You Have a Custom Domain (e.g. `yourname.com` or `journal.yourdomain.com`):\n- You can point your custom domain to any of the above platforms (Render, Vercel, Cloud Run) for free with automatic SSL/HTTPS certificates.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Checklist for Live Hosting:\n1. Keep the code in a **GitHub repository** (for version control and easy syncing).\n2. Deploy to a platform that supports Node.js (Clou