    session_summary: "1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Hosting Deployment Strategy**: The user is deciding on a production hosting environment. While the app is currently running on Google Cloud Run (via AI Studio), the user inquired about using GitHub Pages (which is not suitable for this full-stack app) and is now considering their options for a permanent live host.\n  - Status: NOT STARTED / SUGGESTED.\n  - User Intent: \"WHICH SHOULD I USE FOR MY LIVE HOST ?\"\n\n2. User Knowledge\n- User Email: `bhainirdesh92@gmail.com`\n- Preferences:\n  - Wants a trading journal that uses Notion as the primary database for \"unlimited storage.\"\n  - Requires Google Auth for secure, private sessions.\n  - Wants to ensure the app is fully functional as a live, hosted application.\n- Key Quotes:\n  - \"NOW CAN I HAVE MY JOURNAL ENTRY FROM NOTION OR I SHOULD USE THIS APP FOR JOURNAL ?\"\n  - \"THOS APP WILL GIVE ME NOW UNLIMITED STORAGE OR NOT?\"\n  - \"I SHOULD USE GITHUB DOMAIN FOR LIVE HOST RIGHT?\"\n  - \"WHICH SHOULD I USE FOR MY LIVE HOST ?\"\n\n3. Work Accomplished\n- **Migration to Notion**: Successfully migrated the entire application backend from Supabase to Notion.\n- **Full 2-Way Sync**: Implemented `src/lib/notion.ts` to handle reading, writing, updating, and deleting trades directly in a Notion database.\n- **UI/UX Implementation**:\n  - Created `src/components/NotionSettingsModal.tsx` for database configuration and sync status.\n  - Created `src/components/LoginPanel.tsx` supporting Google Auth, Demo mode, and Notion-only mode.\n  - Created `src/components/Header.tsx` with integrated Notion status and account management.\n  - Created `src/App.tsx` to orchestrate state between local storage, Notion, and UI components.\n- **Backend Fix**: Resolved a TypeScript error in `server.ts` regarding the Notion client query method by casting to `any` to bypass strict type checking for the specific database query implementation.\n- **Cleanup**: Deleted `/src/lib/supabase.ts` as it is no longer required.\n- **Environment**: Created `/.env.example` defining required keys (`GEMINI_API_KEY`, `NOTION_API_KEY`, `NOTION_DATABASE_ID`, `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`).\n\n4. Model Knowledge\n- **Architecture**:\n  - Frontend: React (Vite) managing state for trades and configuration.\n  - Backend: Node.js/Express (`server.ts`) acting as a proxy to the Notion API and Gemini AI. This is required to keep API keys secure.\n  - Persistence: Notion Database is the primary source of truth. LocalStorage is used for caching and session management.\n- **Constraints**:\n  - GitHub Pages is a static host and cannot run the `server.ts` backend.\n  - The application requires a Node.js-capable hosting environment (e.g., Google Cloud Run, Render, Vercel, Railway).\n- **Failures**:\n  - Initial `server.ts` implementation failed due to strict TypeScript checking on the Notion SDK `databases.query` method. Resolved by casting the client to `any` for the query call.\n\n5. Files and Code\n- **Edited/Created Files**:\n  - `/src/lib/notion.ts`: Core logic for Notion API interaction.\n  - `/src/lib/auth.ts`: Authentication logic and user session management.\n  - `/src/components/NotionSettingsModal.tsx`: UI for Notion integration.\n  - `/src/components/LoginPanel.tsx`: Authentication UI.\n  - `/src/components/Header.tsx`: Navigation and global status.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Main application entry point and state management.\n  - `/server.ts`: Backend API routes.\n  - `/.env.example`: Template for required environment variables.\n- **Deleted Files**:\n  - `/src/lib/supabase.ts`: Removed as part of the migration.\n- **Viewed Files (Relevant for next agent)**:\n  - `/server.ts`: Contains the API endpoints. Crucial for deployment configuration.\n  - `/src/App.tsx`: Central hub for state. Read this to understand how the app initializes.\n\n6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current State**: The application is fully functional and currently running on a temporary Google Cloud Run URL.\n- **Next Steps**:\n  - If the user decides to move to a permanent host (like Render or Vercel), assist them with the deployment configuration (environment variables, build commands).\n  - Ensure the user has successfully saved their Notion API keys in the production environment\'s settings.\n  - No further code changes are required for the core functionality at this time."
