  planner_response {
    response: "**Yes, exactly!** \n\nHere are the 2 easiest ways to push this code to your GitHub:\n\n---\n\n### Method A: One-Click Export from AI Studio (Easiest)\n1. In the top-right corner of Google AI Studio, click the **Settings / Menu** icon (or **Export** button).\n2. Click **\"Export to GitHub\"** (or **\"Download ZIP\"** if you prefer to upload manually).\n3. Select your GitHub account and choose a repository name (e.g. `trading-journal-notion`).\n4. AI Studio will automatically create the repository and push all your files to GitHub.\n\n---\n\n### Method B: Via Terminal / Git CLI (If downloading ZIP)\nIf you download the project ZIP file:\n1. Extract the ZIP on your computer and open a terminal in the folder.\n2. Run these standard commands:\n```bash\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit of Notion Trading Journal\"\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n### Next Step After Pushing to GitHub:\nOnce your code is in your GitHub repository, you can log into **[render.com](https://render.com)** (or **[vercel.com](https://vercel.com)**), select the repository, and click **Deploy**!"
    modified_response: "**Yes, exactly!** \n\nHere are the 2 easiest ways to push this code to your GitHub:\n\n---\n\n### Method A: One-Click Export from AI Studio (Easiest)\n1. In the top-right corner of Google AI Studio, click the **Settings / Menu** icon (or **Export** button).\n2. Click **\"Export to GitHub\"** (or **\"Download ZIP\"** if you prefer to upload manually).\n3. Select your GitHub account and choose a repository name (e.g. `trading-journal-notion`).\n4. AI Studio will automatically create the repository and push all your files to GitHub.\n\n---\n\n### Method B: Via Terminal / Git CLI (If downloading ZIP)\nIf you download the project ZIP file:\n1. Extract the ZIP on your computer and open a terminal in the folder.\n2. Run these standard commands:\n```bash\ngit init\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"Initial commit of Notion Trading Journal\"\ngit branch -M main\ngit remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_REPO_NAME.git\ngit push -u origin main\n```\n\n---\n\n### Next Step After Pushing to GitHub:\nOnce your code is in your GitHub repository, you can log into **[render.com](https://render.com)** (or **[vercel.com](https://vercel.com)**), select the repository, and click **Deploy**!"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
