  planner_response {
    response: "In Google AI Studio, you can push or export your code directly using the top interface:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: One-Click Export to GitHub (Built-in)\n\n1. Look at the **top-right navigation bar** of this AI Studio screen.\n2. Click the **`...` (Menu)** or **Settings** icon (next to Share / Deploy).\n3. Select **\"Export to GitHub\"** (or **\"Connect to GitHub\"**).\n4. Authorize your GitHub account when prompted, pick a repository name (e.g., `notion-trading-journal`), and click **Export**.\n5. AI Studio will automatically create the repo and push all project files directly to your GitHub account!\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Download as ZIP\n\nIf you prefer to download the code to your computer first:\n1. In the same top-right menu, select **\"Download ZIP\"** / **\"Export ZIP\"**.\n2. Extract the folder on your computer.\n3. On GitHub.com, create a new repository called `trading-journal`.\n4. Drag and drop the extracted files into GitHub or run `git push` from your terminal.\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Terminal Git Push (Using Personal Access Token)\n\nIf you already have an empty GitHub repository created on your account (e.g. `https://github.com/username/trading-journal`), you can share your **GitHub repository URL** and a **GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)**, or run standard Git commands to push immediately."
    modified_response: "In Google AI Studio, you can push or export your code directly using the top interface:\n\n---\n\n### Option 1: One-Click Export to GitHub (Built-in)\n\n1. Look at the **top-right navigation bar** of this AI Studio screen.\n2. Click the **`...` (Menu)** or **Settings** icon (next to Share / Deploy).\n3. Select **\"Export to GitHub\"** (or **\"Connect to GitHub\"**).\n4. Authorize your GitHub account when prompted, pick a repository name (e.g., `notion-trading-journal`), and click **Export**.\n5. AI Studio will automatically create the repo and push all project files directly to your GitHub account!\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Download as ZIP\n\nIf you prefer to download the code to your computer first:\n1. In the same top-right menu, select **\"Download ZIP\"** / **\"Export ZIP\"**.\n2. Extract the folder on your computer.\n3. On GitHub.com, create a new repository called `trading-journal`.\n4. Drag and drop the extracted files into GitHub or run `git push` from your terminal.\n\n---\n\n### Option 3: Terminal Git Push (Using Personal Access Token)\n\nIf you already have an empty GitHub repository created on your account (e.g. `https://github.com/username/trading-journal`), you can share your **GitHub repository URL** and a **GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT)**, or run standard Git commands to push immediately."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
