    response: "If you export to **Antigravity** (Google\'s AI coding workspace):\n\n---\n\n### What happens when you export to Antigravity:\n\n1. **Seamless Transfer of Full Codebase**:\n   - All your files, components, setups (`DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, `T.C. QML A+`, `DB`, `DT`), Notion API routes, and styling are imported directly into your Antigravity workspace.\n\n2. **Full Development Environment**:\n   - You get an active container terminal, live preview, file editor, and direct integration with Git/GitHub.\n\n3. **Direct GitHub Push from Antigravity**:\n   - Inside Antigravity, you can open the built-in terminal or Source Control tab to connect directly to your GitHub account and run `git push` in one click.\n\n4. **Continued AI Iteration**:\n   - You can continue asking the agent to refine features, add charts, or customize your Notion database schema anytime.\n\n---\n\n### What to do after exporting to Antigravity:\n1. Click **Export to Antigravity**.\n2. Once opened, check that your environment variables (`NOTION_API_KEY`, `NOTION_DATABASE_ID`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) are set in the settings or `.env`.\n3. Link your GitHub account in Antigravity to push your repository and deploy to **Render**, **Vercel**, or **Cloud Run**."
    modified_response: "If you export to **Antigravity** (Google\'s AI coding workspace):\n\n---\n\n### What happens when you export to Antigravity:\n\n1. **Seamless Transfer of Full Codebase**:\n   - All your files, components, setups (`DEMAND`, `SUPPLY`, `T.C QML`, `T.C. QML A+`, `DB`, `DT`), Notion API routes, and styling are imported directly into your Antigravity workspace.\n\n2. **Full Development Environment**:\n   - You get an active container terminal, live preview, file editor, and direct integration with Git/GitHub.\n\n3. **Direct GitHub Push from Antigravity**:\n   - Inside Antigravity, you can open the built-in terminal or Source Control tab to connect directly to your GitHub account and run `git push` in one click.\n\n4. **Continued AI Iteration**:\n   - You can continue asking the agent to refine features, add charts, or customize your Notion database schema anytime.\n\n---\n\n### What to do after exporting to Antigravity:\n1. Click **Export to Antigravity**.\n2. Once opened, check that your environment variables (`NOTION_API_KEY`, `NOTION_DATABASE_ID`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`) are set in the settings or `.env`.\n3. Link your GitHub account in Antigravity to push your repository and deploy to **Render**, **Vercel**, or **Cloud Run**."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
